{"title":"4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Four</b> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> preceding <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Five\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Five\">five</a> and following <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Three\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Three\">three</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Four is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">square</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a35631e1e126934ead6d2af161e9d250827bbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Four-color_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Four-color Theorem (page does not exist)\">Four-color Theorem</a> states that four is the largest integer such that any map can be colored using that number of colors and no two regions of the map share a border and have the same color.</li>\n<li>It is the smallest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Semiprime\" title=\"Semiprime\">semiprime</a>/biprime (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c044326e2e84b768dafef07060bd42b0a5cb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />) and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Composite_number\" title=\"Composite number\">composite number</a>.</li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=4&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194819\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 19/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 244/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 325/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.492      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.492      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30853:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017194819 and revision id 289736. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}